ine to the `[rendering]` section of the project.godot file:\n> \n> `rendering_device/driver.macos=\"vulkan\"`\n\nThis worked for me too, thank you.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5634052003/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5634071282","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123394#issuecomment-5634071282","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123394","id":5634071282,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT9Ea8g","user":{"login":"quitelight","id":139787492,"node_id":"U_kgDOCFT85A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/139787492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight","html_url":"https://github.com/quitelight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/quitelight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T11:56:44Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T11:56:44Z","body":"> Temporary solution: Add this line to the `[rendering]` section of the project.godot file:\n> \n> `rendering_device/driver.macos=\"vulkan\"`\n\nI wanted to add that prior adding this line, the rendering section looked like this:\n\n<img width=\"615\" height=\"110\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/729877b6-b5df-48de-93a0-5f8fa2fc4671\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5634071282/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5635232200","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123394#issuecomment-5635232200","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123394","id":5635232200,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT-LRyA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T13:36:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T13:36:33Z","body":"Seems like it is caused by https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122248\n\nSpecifically failing on this assert: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/cb41ea115914c61a8329087b4cffbad7477b8427/thirdparty/offset_allocator/offsetAllocator.cpp#L298\n\nNot sure what's exactly causing it, it is not reproducible under debugger or if a few prints added to free function, but seems like it's trying to free something that was not allocated.\n\ncc @stuartcarnie\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5635232200/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5641850033","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123394#issuecomment-5641850033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123394","id":5641850033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUEfMsQ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-11T23:36:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T23:36:06Z","body":"@bruvzg you're right – the official build is crashing for me, but a [CI build from the main branch](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/34653939629/artifacts/10285407486) is fine.\n\n> [!NOTE]\n>\n> I used a 🤖 to help diagnose the issue.\n\nThe official binary's `MetalHeapAllocator::_free_allocation` has no `Kind::INVALID` branch (which is testing for 0).\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c24bf5d933c53d9477d5e82c51403856a9e7da62/drivers/metal/metal_allocator.cpp#L244-L250\n\nCompiled prologue of `_free_allocation`:\n\n```asm\nldrb   w21, [x1]              ; kind\nldrb   w9, [x1, #1]           ; pool\numaddl x23, w9, w8, x0        ; &pools[pool]\nbl     os_unfair_lock_lock    ; lock taken BEFORE switch, unconditionally\ncmp    w21, #0x2\nb.ne   <POOL path>            ; anything != DEDICATED goes to POOL\n```\n\nUsing `lldb` to look at the disassembled code and registers:\n\n- Real crash site is OffsetAllocator::Allocator::free + 40, called from _free_allocation + 204 (POOL path). Bad address = m_nodes + 0xffffffff * 28, i.e. metadata == NO_SPACE.\n- MetalAllocation passed in (24 bytes at x19):\n\n```\nkind=0x00 (INVALID) pool=0 block=0 alloc={0xffffffff,0xffffffff} heap=nullptr\n```\n\nThis is a default handle that should be ignored. Often the result of creating a texture view from `texture_create_shared`.\n\nThere is no compare against 0 anywhere in the function. The POOL path: allocationSize returns 0 (guards NO_SPACE), then `free()` indexes `m_nodes[0xffffffff]` and faults.\n\nApple clang keeps the branch. Unclear yet whether upstream clang is mis-compiling or performing some other optimisation.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5641850033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5642059281","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123394#issuecomment-5642059281","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123394","id":5642059281,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUEr-EQ","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T00:10:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T00:10:25Z","body":"Summary from 🤖 (and my edits) after comparing Apple clang output with llvm@21.\n\nThe root cause is not a compiler bug. Undefined behaviour in metal-cpp's `NS::SharedPtr`, exploited by upstream LLVM but not by Apple clang.\n\n**Mechanism**\n\n`~SharedPtr` in `thirdparty/metal-cpp/Foundation/NSSharedPtr.hpp` line 170:\n\n```cpp\n_NS_INLINE NS::SharedPtr<_Class>::~SharedPtr<_Class>() __attribute__((no_sanitize(\"undefined\")))\n{\n    m_pObject->release();\n}\n```\n\nNo null check. Calling a member function through a null pointer is UB. Clang tags `this` as `nonnull`. In `_free_allocation`, `old_heap` is a default-constructed `SharedPtr`, and on the `INVALID` path it is provably null at the destructor. LLVM concludes that path is unreachable and deletes the `case INVALID` edge. Every remaining path locks a pool, so the lock gets hoisted above the switch. Result: `INVALID` handles fall into the POOL path, `free(NO_SPACE)` indexes `m_nodes[0xffffffff]`, crash. The `no_sanitize(\"undefined\")` attribute suppresses the sanitizer, not the optimizer.\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n>\n> `m_pObject->release()` is not actually UB, as Apple's Metal headers don't ever dereference `this`. All calls are through Objective-C message send, and it is valid to send a message to a `nil` object in Objective-C:\n>\n> https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/c24bf5d933c53d9477d5e82c51403856a9e7da62/thirdparty/metal-cpp/Foundation/NSObject.hpp#L113-L117\n>\n> `this` only passes the pointer, and the Objective-C runtime checks for `nil` and simply returns.\n\n**How the 🤖 validated it**\n\n- Homebrew clang 21.1.8, `-O3`, main's source: reproduces official codegen exactly. Same at `-O1`, `-O2`, `-Os`.\n- `-O0` IR still has the full three-way switch. The optimizer removes it.\n- Apple clang 21.0.0, identical flags: keeps the branch. Matches the CI binary you provided, which also ran clean.\n- `-fno-delete-null-pointer-checks` with clang 21: branch restored.\n- Null check added to `~SharedPtr` only, clang 21: branch restored.\n\n**Other unguarded derefs in the same header**, all potentially the same hazard:\n\n| Line     | Function             |\n| -------- | -------------------- |\n| 170      | destructor           |\n| 181      | copy constructor     |\n| 228      | `reset()`            |\n| 243      | copy assignment      |\n| 269, 275 | `operator=` variants |\n| 288      | move assignment      |\n\n\n**The 🤖 recommended the following fix** \n\nGuard every `m_pObject->` call in `NSSharedPtr.hpp` with a null check, shipped as a metal-cpp patch. Safer than `-fno-delete-null-pointer-checks` because any default-constructed `SharedPtr` destroyed on a provably-null path anywhere in the driver can hit this. The `_free_allocation` early return I suggested earlier only masks this one site.\n\nI'm still evaluating solutions, as there are a few. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5642059281/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5643225081","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123394#issuecomment-5643225081","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123394","id":5643225081,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABUFzH-Q","user":{"login":"stuartcarnie","id":52852,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyODUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52852?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-12T03:40:02Z","updated_at":"2026-09-12T03:40:02Z","body":"I've fixed it in #123439","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5643225081/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://a